.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE-ADD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine-add - Print Linux/macOS and Windows machine enrollment commands


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine add [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the one-shot commands that enroll a new machine: one for Linux and macOS, one for
Windows. Run the printed command on the new machine soon after: the enrollment token in it is
single-use and expires (--json shows expires_at). With --workspace the token
is for that workspace. --name suggests the machine's hostname.

.PP
If the printed commands cannot be shown, the unused enrollment is cancelled again.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	optional machine hostname


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb machine add
  pb machine add --name db-1
  pb machine add --workspace acme --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-machine(1)\fP
